---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const breadcrumbItems = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Cookie Policy', url: '/cookie-policy' }
];
---

<Layout 
  title="Cookie Policy & Privacy Controls"
  description="Cookie Policy explaining essential, analytical, and preference cookies used on the Edgar Valle Real Estate platform under California privacy laws."
  canonicalUrl="/cookie-policy"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbItems}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbItems} />
  <div class="section">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <div class="section-header" style="text-align: left; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
        <span class="section-eyebrow">PRIVACY &amp; TRANSPARENCY</span>
        <h1>Cookie Policy &amp; Consent Controls</h1>
        <p class="lead">Last Updated: October 2026. Learn how we use cookies, local storage, and privacy controls under California privacy law (CCPA/CPRA).</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="padding: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);">
          <div>
            <h3 style="margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;">Your Active Consent Status</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">You can modify or withdraw your cookie preferences at any time.</p>
          </div>
          <button type="button" id="openCookieSettingsBtn" class="btn btn-gold btn-sm">
            Manage Cookie Preferences
          </button>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">1. What Are Cookies and Local Storage?</h3>
        <p>
          Cookies and local storage are standard web technologies that store small amounts of information directly in your browser. This enables websites to recognize your device, remember preferences (such as your chosen language or property filter criteria), and safeguard administrative logins against unauthorized access.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">2. Categorized Cookie Inventory</h3>
        <p>We believe in total transparency. Below is an inventory of cookies and browser storage keys used on this platform:</p>

        <div style="overflow-x: auto; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
          <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; text-align: left;">
            <thead>
              <tr style="background: var(--bg-surface); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border-light);">
                <th style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Identifier</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Category</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Provider</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Purpose</th>
                <th style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Retention</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);">
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-family: monospace;">valle_admin_session</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;"><span class="badge badge-gold" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Strictly Necessary</span></td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">1st Party (Server)</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Cryptographically signed HTTP-only cookie protecting the Realtor admin portal against session hijacking.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">24 Hours</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);">
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-family: monospace;">valle_cookie_consent</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;"><span class="badge badge-gold" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Strictly Necessary</span></td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">1st Party (Local Storage)</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Stores your accepted privacy preferences (essential, analytics, marketing) to respect your choice across visits.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">12 Months</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);">
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-family: monospace;">valle_anon_sid</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;"><span class="badge badge-blue" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Analytics</span></td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">1st Party (Session Storage)</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Randomized session identifier to understand aggregate listing engagement. Never correlates with your name or email. Active only if consented.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Browser Session</td>
              </tr>
              <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-light);">
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem; font-family: monospace;">sb-*-auth-token</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;"><span class="badge badge-gold" style="font-size: 0.75rem;">Strictly Necessary</span></td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Supabase Auth</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Authenticated JWT tokens for authorized administrative database interactions.</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.75rem 1rem;">Session / Expired on Logout</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3. California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA / CPRA) Rights</h3>
        <p>
          Under the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA), California consumers have the right to opt-out of the "sale" or "sharing" of personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Edgar Valle does not sell your personal data or share your information with commercial advertising networks.</strong> You can disable all non-essential analytics and marketing tracking by selecting "Essential Only" in the cookie preferences modal above.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">4. Managing Cookies in Your Browser</h3>
        <p>
          In addition to our on-site consent controls, you can restrict or delete cookies through your web browser settings. Please visit the official guidance for your browser:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin: 0 0 1.25rem 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary);">
          <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--color-gold-700);">Google Chrome Cookie Guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--color-gold-700);">Apple Safari Cookie Guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clear-cookies-and-site-data-firefox" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--color-gold-700);">Mozilla Firefox Cookie Guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--color-gold-700);">Microsoft Edge Cookie Guide</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
  var openBtn = document.getElementById('openCookieSettingsBtn');
  if (openBtn) {
    openBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('valle-open-cookie-settings'));
    });
  }
</script>
